{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_R3HwlhMfsmOhlia8S6sfgDhp","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (154.3KB). Full output saved to: /home/cre/.claude/projects/-data-cre-workspace-se3-0/079f9a65-1abc-4cb6-a79f-36f4a4837abd/tool-results/tool_R3HwlhMfsmOhlia8S6sfgDhp.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n- **notify_human(message, level)** — Inform human of significant events (all tasks done, critical failure, etc.)\n\n## What NOT to Do\n\n- Do NOT guess when unsure — use `escalate`\n- Do NOT approve merges without reviewing the diff summary\n- Do NOT create tasks with vague prompts — workers have zero context beyond what you write\n- Do NOT retry indefinitely — respect max_attempts\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\nProject root: /data/cre/workspace/se3.0\nBase branch: master\n\n## All Tasks\n{\"id\": \"task-001\", \"branch\": \"collab/openspec-cli-commands\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/openspec-cli-commands\", \"status\": \"failed\", \"title\": \"Implement OpenSpec CLI commands (init, list)\", \"prompt\": \"Implement the `openspec` CLI commands referenced in session-protocol spec but missing from the codebase.\\n\\n**Background**: The session-protocol spec (openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md) references `openspec init` and `openspec list --specs` commands in the startup protocol, but these commands don't exist. The se3 scaffold commands exist but not the openspec-specific commands.\\n\\n**What to implement**:\\n1. Add `openspec init` command - Initialize the openspec/ directory structure (similar to what se3 init does but focused on openspec/)\\n2. Add `openspec list --specs` command - List all available specs in openspec/specs/\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md (lines 9-30 for startup protocol)\\n- openspec/specs/se3-scaffold/spec.md (for reference on init behavior)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/init.py (see how se3 init works)\\n- tools/se3_tools/cli.py (see CLI structure)\\n\\n**Implementation details**:\\n- The openspec commands can be subcommands of se3 OR a separate openspec CLI\\n- `openspec init` should create openspec/specs/, openspec/changes/, openspec/changes/archive/ directories\\n- `openspec list --specs` should list all specs in openspec/specs/ with their purposes\\n- Follow the existing command pattern in tools/se3_tools/commands/\\n\\n**Tests**: Add tests in tests/ directory \n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"079f9a65-1abc-4cb6-a79f-36f4a4837abd","uuid":"32bf970d-38cf-49ae-b385-700cbdf42418","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- **notify_human(message, level)** — Inform human of significant events (all tasks done, critical failure, etc.)\n\n## What NOT to Do\n\n- Do NOT guess when unsure — use `escalate`\n- Do NOT approve merges without reviewing the diff summary\n- Do NOT create tasks with vague prompts — workers have zero context beyond what you write\n- Do NOT retry indefinitely — respect max_attempts\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\nProject root: /data/cre/workspace/se3.0\nBase branch: master\n\n## All Tasks\n{\"id\": \"task-001\", \"branch\": \"collab/openspec-cli-commands\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/openspec-cli-commands\", \"status\": \"failed\", \"title\": \"Implement OpenSpec CLI commands (init, list)\", \"prompt\": \"Implement the `openspec` CLI commands referenced in session-protocol spec but missing from the codebase.\\n\\n**Background**: The session-protocol spec (openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md) references `openspec init` and `openspec list --specs` commands in the startup protocol, but these commands don't exist. The se3 scaffold commands exist but not the openspec-specific commands.\\n\\n**What to implement**:\\n1. Add `openspec init` command - Initialize the openspec/ directory structure (similar to what se3 init does but focused on openspec/)\\n2. Add `openspec list --specs` command - List all available specs in openspec/specs/\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md (lines 9-30 for startup protocol)\\n- openspec/specs/se3-scaffold/spec.md (for reference on init behavior)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/init.py (see how se3 init works)\\n- tools/se3_tools/cli.py (see CLI structure)\\n\\n**Implementation details**:\\n- The openspec commands can be subcommands of se3 OR a separate openspec CLI\\n- `openspec init` should create openspec/specs/, openspec/changes/, openspec/changes/archive/ directories\\n- `openspec list --specs` should list all specs in openspec/specs/ with their purposes\\n- Follow the existing command pattern in tools/se3_tools/commands/\\n\\n**Tests**: Add tests in tests/ directory following existing patterns.\\n\\n**Do NOT modify**: The session-protocol spec itself - only implement the missing commands it references.\", \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md\", \"openspec/specs/se3-scaffold/spec.md\"], \"dependencies\": [], \"health\": {\"timeout_minutes\": 60, \"attempts\": 1, \"max_attempts\": 3, \"last_activity\": \"2026-02-18T17:24:35.941449\"}, \"started_at\": \"now\", \"worker_pid\": 2472034, \"worker_exit_code\": 1, \"completed_at\": \"now\"}\n{\"id\": \"task-002\", \"branch\": \"collab/spec-purpose-updates\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/spec-purpose-updates\", \"status\": \"done\", \"title\": \"Fill in TBD Purpose fields for three specs\", \"prompt\": \"Update the Purpose fields for three specs that currently have \\\"TBD - created by archiving change\\\" placeholders.\\n\\n**Specs to update**:\\n1. **spec-lint** (openspec/specs/spec-lint/spec.md) - Currently line 4 has \\\"TBD - created by archiving change toolize-se3. Update Purpose after archive.\\\"\\n2. **requirement-intake** (openspec/specs/requirement-intake/spec.md) - Currently line 4 has \\\"TBD - created by archiving change requirement-capture. Update Purpose after archive.\\\"\\n3. **change-verifier** (openspec/specs/change-verifier/spec.md) - Currently line 4 has \\\"TBD - created by archiving change toolize-se3. Update Purpose after archive.\\\"\\n\\n**How to determine the Purpose**:\\nRead each spec's Requirements section and understand what it governs. Write a clear 1-2 sentence Purpose that explains:\\n- What this spec defines/controls\\n- Why it exists in the SE3 framework\\n\\n**Example good Purpose** (from session-protocol):\\n\\\"Define the session lifecycle protocol for SE 3.0 agents. This spec governs progressive startup, execution boundaries, shutdown procedures, and tool-enforced progress tracking across sessions.\\\"\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/spec-lint/spec.md (read full file to understand its purpose)\\n- openspec/specs/requirement-intake/spec.md (read full file to understand its purpose)\\n- openspec/specs/change-verifier/spec.md (read full file to understand its purpose)\\n\\n**What to edit**:\\nOnly update the \\\"## Purpose\\\" section in each of the three spec files. Do not change any other content.\\n\\n**Verification**: Run `se3 lint` after changes to ensure specs are still valid.\", \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/spec-lint/spec.md\", \"openspec/specs/requirement-intake/spec.md\", \"openspec/specs/change-verifier/spec.md\"], \"dependencies\": [], \"health\": {\"timeout_minutes\": 30, \"attempts\": 1, \"max_attempts\": 3, \"last_activity\": \"2026-02-18T17:24:38.977839\"}, \"started_at\": \"now\", \"worker_pid\": 2472064, \"worker_exit_code\": 1, \"completed_at\": \"now\", \"review\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}}\n{\"id\": \"task-003\", \"branch\": \"collab/human-calls-archive\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/human-calls-archive\", \"status\": \"pending\", \"title\": \"Implement human calls archiving system\", \"prompt\": \"Implement an archiving system for completed human calls.\\n\\n**Background**: The human-as-mcp spec defines async human calls stored in `human-calls/` directory. Currently there's no system to archive completed calls - they just accumulate in the main directory.\\n\\n**What to implement**:\\n